			"notes": "Host your singleplayer world for friends anywhere: one fixed address, no port forwarding, no server.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- **Your own address** like `mossy-otter-27.vibey.henny.dev`. It stays the same every time you host, until you renew it.\n- **Host World** in the pause menu: address, status, start/stop. Nothing else.\n- **Manage** menu:\n  - **Players:** OP, kick, ban, and \"recently turned away\" with one-click \"Let in\"\n  - **Access:** whitelist and ban list (name or IP), enforced by the relay on network level\n  - **World:** game mode, cheats, PvP, max players, force mods\n  - **Advanced:** exact mod versions, new address, own relay server\n- **Friends don't need the mod.** They join through *Multiplayer → Direct Connection* (unless *Force mods* is on).\n- English and German.\n\n## Which file?\n\nPick the jar for your loader and Minecraft version. Fabric also needs [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api). Client only.\n\n| Minecraft | Fabric | NeoForge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1.21, 1.21.1 | `fabric-1.21-1.21.1` | `neoforge-1.21-1.21.1` |\n| 1.21.2, 1.21.3 | `fabric-1.21.2-1.21.3` | `neoforge-1.21.2-1.21.3` |\n| 1.21.4 | `fabric-1.21.4` | `neoforge-1.21.4` |\n| 1.21.5 | `fabric-1.21.5` | `neoforge-1.21.5` |\n| 1.21.6 – 1.21.8 | `fabric-1.21.6-1.21.8` | `neoforge-1.21.6-1.21.8` |\n| 1.21.9, 1.21.10 | `fabric-1.21.9-1.21.10` | `neoforge-1.21.9-1.21.10` |\n| 1.21.11 | `fabric-1.21.11` | `neoforge-1.21.11` |\n| 26.1 | `fabric-26.1` | `neoforge-26.1` |\n| 26.2 | `fabric-26.2` | `neoforge-26.2` |\n| 26.3 | `fabric-26.3` | `neoforge-26.3` |\n\nRelay status: https://vibey-status.henny.dev/status"
		}
	],
